\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 \strokec2 ENDING:
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 Mira falls on the floor, and quickly stands up. As she gets up, she sees two officials, dressed in all black with shocked expressions, staring right at her.\'a0
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93Hey! What are you doing here!?\'94 said the first official in an aggressive tone
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'94And how much have you heard!?\'94 added the second one
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'94Nothing\'85 I just got lost going to the bathroom and heard voices so I came in\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'94No one gets lost here, you are in great trouble\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 Without a second thought, Mira dashed towards and out the door, down the hallway, in an attempt to escape.\'a0
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93HEY! GET BACK HERE!\'94 Screamed the first official
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 She kept running to not be caught, was this how Sarah had gone missing? Was it because she knew too much? She didn\'92t even want to think about it, she was so flustered, but let out a large sigh of relief when she saw Torin leaning against the wall on the other end of the hallway.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'94Mira!\'94 He screamed from across the room.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 She ran towards him
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93Torin! Quickly I need to hide!\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 Without hesitation, Torin opened the metal door beside him, let Mira in, and rapidly closed the door behind them. They heard footsteps and thuds running past the door and then heard them abruptly end at the end of the hallway.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'94We lost them\'94 said the official
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'94Do you know who the girl was? We can\'92t let the truth get out, we have to find her!\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 Once they were sure the officials had left, one of them finally spoke.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'94Mira, you have to tell me what the hell is going on!?\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'94Torin, it's all fake, it's all lies, everything that they\'92ve told us about the surface being unsafe, about the radiation being deadly, the government made up everything to keep us contained!\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93Wha..t, how do you know?\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 She told him about everything, the radiation reports, Sarah\'92s disappearance, the conversation she heard while listening through the door.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'94You heard them say there\'92s no radiation?\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'94Yes. Did you know that there wasn\'92t any radiation, that it was all false?\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93Not exactly\'94 Torin sighed, \'93but I had my suspicions, how could there have been fish, plants, and a clear sky if the radiation was deadly. The only reason I hadn\'92t said anything is because I was afraid of being punished, I doubted myself because I thought I would be called crazy\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'94We need to expose them\'94 Mira said, \'93we can\'92t keep living like this!\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 Yeah, but we need more evidence, if we don\'92t gather more, no one will believe us\'94\'a0
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93Yeah, you are right\'94 replied Mira, \'93if we don\'92t have concrete evidence, it will turn into a game of he said, she said. But how do we let everyone know?\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93We can use the abandoned communications room, we just need to pick the lock and we can broadcast the evidence to the whole tank.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 The next day, Mira, once again, asks Miss River to go to the bathroom, making sure to keep her phone hidden in her pocket.\'a0
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93Yes Mira, you may use the restroom\'94\'a0
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 Instantly, Mira got up and paced towards the door of the class. Once she was sure she was out of sight, she sprinted down the stairs, back to where she had heard the official\'92s voices the previous day. There it was, the same door, saying NO ENTRY, she waited, with her ear to the door, but making sure not to lean so she wouldn\'92t collapse it like last time. After one minute she heard no voices and concluded it was empty.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 Paranoid of being caught, she sneakily walked in, and found more radiation reports, all with the same level of radiation and conclusion. \'93ZERO RADIATION FOUND, ENVIRONMENT IS HABITABLE\'94.\'a0
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 She put the radiation reports in her backpack and then suddenly heard echoing voices approaching from the hallway. Instinctively, she hid in the nearest closet she found, all in an attempt to not get caught. She heard footsteps reach the door and soon after heard someone shouting. As she looked through the hole between the closet and the wall, she saw President Veyr and the two officials from yesterday besides her.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93WHAT THE HELL? HOW DID SHE GET AWAY?\'94 Screamed President Veyr
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'94Sorry mam, we tried to catch her, but she escaped\'94 murmured one of the officials.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'94WHY DID YOU NOT ID HER, AND WHY DID YOU JUST TELL ME THIS TODAY! NOW WE HAVE NO LEADS, AND SHE MAY VERY WELL BE EXPOSING THE TRUTH RIGHT NOW! \'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 Mira quickly took out her phone as this could be used as evidence to expose the truth.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93Miss President, why does the radiation being zero have to be kept secret, why can't we let humanity explore the surface, and reach the surface?\'93 asked the second official nervously.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'94DON\'92T YOU UNDERSTAND, HUMANITY WILL CEASE TO EXIST IF THEY HAVE ALL THE FREEDOM IN THE WORLD, THEY WILL FIGHT AND HAVE WARS, I NEED TO HELP THEM NOT DESTROY THEMSELVES!\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 Mira had only seen the cool, calm, and collected persona that President Veyr showed herself to be, she had never heard her like this, everything she pretended to be was fake, and she had shown her true intentions while Mira recorded her
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'94Ok, I will need you two to describe the suspect and I will have our most talented sketch artist draw her so we can find a match in the database and prevent this retaliation."
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 At the same time, Torin took a camera, connected it to an antenna, and quickly dove up to the surface. He took it, and propped it up on a rock, where you could see the beautiful sky and the wonderful tropical fish. It was done, Mira and Torin had all they needed to overpower the government and allow humanity to live a peaceful, free life, without control and censorship.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 The officials and the President Veyr quickly left the room in order to have a sketch drawn of Mira. She waited 20 seconds to make sure they were gone, then left the closet, and sprinted up the stairs. As she headed towards the communications room, she heard Torin calling for her.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'94Mira! Mira!\'94 He shouted from the communications room.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 She ran towards him.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'94What took you so long?\'94\'a0
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'93I had to hide in the closet because the President came into the room, and the two officials from the other day\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'94Oh my god! I am so glad you didn\'92t get caught, and did you get the evidence?\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'94Yep, I even have a recording of the President acknowledging there is no radiation, It will prove that they lied to us all this time!\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'94Ok, great, I picked the lock while I was waiting for you, we just need to plug your phone and my camera receiver into the broadcasting system\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 They quickly plugged everything into the system and Mira spoke through the microphone.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 \'94People of the tank, the government has been lying to you for thousands of years, the surface is habitable and there is no radiation. The footage currently playing shows evidence of the surface with alive fishes and a beautiful blue sky. I will now play evidence that shows acknowledgement by President Veyr that there is in fact no radiation\'94
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 As Mira broadcasted the radiation, she heard footsteps and screams all around the tank, and even heard cheering for their bravery. The government tried to stop them, but they were overthrown, they couldn\'92t stop the hundreds of citizens heading towards the surface. Many of the citizens went up to the surface, using the emergency oxygen helmet given by the government, but no one was brave enough to take their helmet off.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 That was until one elderly diver stepped forward and took his helmet off, and he lived, it was official, the surface was breathable.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 Over the next months, humanity slowly adapted to using the surface, and while underwater cities were not fully eliminated, society was finally free.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\

\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec2 One night, Mira sat on a hill, watching a sunset, she had achieved what generations of people had been missing: freedom.
\fs24 \strokec2 \
\
